1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 1]
On the battlefield, Ghislain stands over the fallen commander and demands the right to command. Skovan is stunned that he would ask for that while their soldiers' lives are on the line, and he flatly refuses, saying he cannot hand over the authority the lord gave him, and walks away.

2
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 2]
Ghislain is annoyed, though he admits he would have reacted the same way. Then a huge orc charges at them, roaring, and Skovan orders him to fall back, saying he is still too inexperienced to lead the troops. Ghislain decides he has no choice and readies his sword instead of retreating.

3
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 3]
He charges past a stunned Skovan toward the orc, and Skovan grabs him, shouting and demanding to know what he thinks he is doing. But Skovan freezes at what he is seeing: the orc stands with a sword driven through its head, then crashes to the ground, dead.

4
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 4]
Skovan stares in disbelief, wondering how Ghislain hit its weak spot. Ghislain turns to him and asks, 'Skovan, right? Do you know what the most important thing in battle is?' More orcs roar forward while the soldiers tremble behind their shields. His answer is blunt: there is no hope of winning when the troops are filled with fear — they need momentum.

5
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 5]
He cuts into another orc as Skovan watches, then leaps into the middle of the orcs with his sword raised while the soldiers look on below. He drives his sword into one more, then stands on the fallen orc, blade bloodied, and taunts them: 'Come at me, orcs... I'll kill all of you!'

6
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 6]
The orcs close in around him, and Skovan watches in disbelief, wondering if he is dreaming. Even as a mana user, he says, it is hard for him to do anything — so how is the skinny young master doing all of this?

7
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 7]
Skovan can already tell Ghislain is tired and panting hard. However, he realises Ghislain is dodging with the smallest movements and striking at weak spots with his swordsmanship, like a manaless sword master — or perhaps even something greater.

8
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 8]
Ghislain laughs at the orcs and taunts them, asking if that is all they have got, because he is still not warmed up, and mocking them for not living up to their reputation as a warrior species. But the soldiers panic as all the orcs charge at him, wondering if he is running away.

9
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 9]
The soldiers call out to their commander as Skovan steps forward, wondering what Ghislain is thinking. Running into the orcs and drawing their attention was good, Skovan thinks — but running away now?

10
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 10]
And in that direction lies the edge of a cliff. Skovan realises it with a jolt: a cliff? 'D-don't tell me...!' He orders the troops to raise a shield wall and decides to follow the first son's lead.

11
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 11]
The orcs thunder after Ghislain as he runs ahead of them. He is certain a skilled commander like Skovan has already realised the plan. He would prefer to cut them all down himself, but his stamina cannot handle that — what he has done should be enough for the troops.

12
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 12]
The pursuing orcs charge on, then check in surprise as Skovan and the troops hold their shield wall, spears ready. Ghislain smiles. 'Perfect.' And leaps off the cliff edge as the orcs look on from above.

13
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 13]
Falling, Ghislain gives the signal: 'Now.' Skovan shouts for the troops to push the orcs off the cliff, and the shield formation advances on them at the edge, driving into the orcs as they shout and push them back.

14
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 14]
The orcs are hurled off the cliff, plummeting and crashing below, and the breathless soldiers realise they managed to kill all those orcs.

15
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 15]
But Skovan rushes to the cliff's edge, shouting for the young master. Below, Ghislain is hanging from his sword, driven into the cliff face, holding on with a faint smile on his bloodied face.

16
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 16]
Skovan stares down at him in shock and leans over the edge, calling out, 'Here, grab my hand!' But Ghislain's hand slips from the sword as he admits, 'I can't...' He falls away while Skovan reaches out, shouting for him to hold on.

17
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 17]
Skovan shouts for the young master as Ghislain falls into darkness, and a voice calls, 'Oppa...' It is Elena, calling, 'Ghislain oppa,' and Ghislain whispers, 'Elena...?'

18
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 18]
Shattered memories flash past: a child asking if their mother is gone, thanking him, then angrily turning on him. Ghislain stands alone in the darkness, holding a fragment of those memories, and realises they are his memories of Elena — until she grabs him and pleads, 'Let's go together!'

19
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 19]
Ghislain wakes in bed, a cloth on his forehead, his eyes opening, and lies alone in the quiet room. He realises he is alive, and that they managed to save him. Sitting up, he wonders if it was a dream, but pain jolts through him: his whole body hurts from pushing himself to the limit — and the pain tells him he is still alive.

20
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 20]
A figure enters the doorway, calling him 'Master?' Belinda rushes in, exclaiming that he is awake, and Ghislain recognises her: 'Belinda...?' She scolds him for not leaving the orcs to the soldiers, then Ghislain pulls her into a hug. Startled, she asks what he is doing, and he answers that he is just glad to see her.

21
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 21]
Belinda is his personal tutor, the only one who stayed by his side since he was little despite his idiotic antics. But after his family fell to ruins and she went missing, he could no longer see her, and he never thought he would see her like this — while she wonders why he is so happy when they see each other every day. He resolves to tell her the truth.

22
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 22]
He tells her to listen carefully: a catastrophe will soon strike Perdium. 'The truth is... I died and came back to life...' But Belinda brushes it off, joking that the orcs almost killed him, and warns him that he, not Perdium, is in greater danger if he keeps causing scenes. Ghislain concludes she does not believe him.

23
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 23]
Belinda asks what he would have done if he had been too hurt to even go to the festival. Ghislain repeats, puzzled, 'Festival...?' She reminds him Lady Elena has been waiting to go to the festival with him, a great chance for the two of them to become close again, as he picks up a framed photograph.

24
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 24]
He remembers a festival always happened around this time of year, though in his past life he never had time for festivals because of a traumatic experience. He asks how long until the festival, and Belinda says it is next week, so he has about a week left. Ghislain quietly echoes, 'Week...'

25
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,001
[TRANG 25]
His thoughts turn to the day that changed his life, as a voice at a doorway asks, 'Oppa, are you inside...?' He calls it the memory that continues to haunt him, as Elena pleads with him: 'Please go with me!' And the chapter closes on a chilling reveal: one week later, Elena will die.
